changelog: |
  0.1.0 — initial extraction of the zer0-mistakes page-feedback widget into a
  framework-agnostic web component. Same issue contract (title tag, section
  order, 7000-char URL budget with logs → directive → environment trimming,
  clipboard fallback, hidden marker), same taxonomy, but type labels now map
  onto the fleet issue-pipeline label set (bug/feature/docs/question) so
  widget-filed issues are pipeline-eligible on the next scan. Adapters for
  Jekyll (non-theme sites), React, and Django/Rails. Zero dependencies.
notes: |
  - Vendor fleet-feedback.js into the repo (assets/js, public/, static/js);
    never hot-link the hub.
  - Every label in feedback_types.yml MUST exist in the target repo:
    `gh label list`. GitHub silently drops unknown labels from prefilled URLs.
  - The zer0-mistakes theme keeps its richer Liquid widget; the theme change
    that makes it work on remote_theme consumers (built-in taxonomy fallback,
    UPS-FB-31) is tracked on the roadmap.
